# The pre-commit contract gate is a POSIX sh script. core.autocrlf=true would check it out with
# CRLF endings, and a CRLF shebang fails on any POSIX shell as `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, which
# would make the hook silently absent on every clone rather than visibly broken.
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# LF for shell scripts generally, so the same failure cannot reappear elsewhere.
*.sh text eol=lf

# rustfmt output is LF, and rustfmt decides pass/fail. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout would otherwise
# smudge .rs to CRLF, and `cargo fmt --all --check` would report a diff on every line of every file, making
# the formatting gate depend on the checkout's settings rather than on the code.
*.rs text eol=lf